1
00:00:02,930 --> 00:00:05,626
Every large enterprise gets assets back:

2
00:00:05,626 --> 00:00:09,401
end-of-lease equipment, returns, retired fleet, surplus.

3
00:00:09,401 --> 00:00:11,761
Each one is a decision worth money.

4
00:00:11,761 --> 00:00:15,940
This is Circularity, the agentic decision layer that makes it.

5
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:19,222
An executive doesn't start with dashboards.

6
00:00:19,222 --> 00:00:20,774
They start with a briefing:

7
00:00:20,774 --> 00:00:29,110
two point four million dollars recovered, one point seven million of new purchases avoided, and where value is at risk right now, with its owner.

8
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:34,090
Every answer shows the tools the agent called, so no number is taken on trust.

9
00:00:36,990 --> 00:00:39,960
Your systems already run every step of a return:

10
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:44,663
the contract, the authorisation, the transport, the receipt, the inspection.

11
00:00:44,663 --> 00:00:49,365
None of them decides the asset's best next life across all of that evidence.

12
00:00:49,365 --> 00:00:54,810
Circularity sits at exactly that moment, and hands the work back to the systems you run.

13
00:00:55,830 --> 00:01:01,430
For the planner, the agent has already prepared twenty-one decisions, and ranked what needs a person.

14
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:09,674
One returned motor.

15
00:01:09,674 --> 00:01:13,075
Seven possible next lives, compared on one economic basis.

16
00:01:13,075 --> 00:01:22,398
Redeploying it against a customer's replacement order is worth ninety-six hundred dollars, forty-eight hundred more than selling it, with a range, not a guess.

17
00:01:22,398 --> 00:01:25,622
One route is ruled out before price is even considered:

18
00:01:25,622 --> 00:01:28,730
there is no confirmed buyer, so the gate excludes it.

19
00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:31,664
Ask it why.

20
00:01:31,664 --> 00:01:38,738
It calls the rules, the prediction models, and the evidence, each one labelled retrieved, model, or rules.

21
00:01:38,738 --> 00:01:41,140
And it drafts the rationale for you.

22
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:47,667
It already shows what will be sent where, once it's approved.

23
00:01:47,667 --> 00:01:48,974
The planner submits.

24
00:01:48,974 --> 00:01:49,955
Agents prepare.

25
00:01:49,955 --> 00:01:50,870
People commit.

26
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:52,769
Now the approver:

27
00:01:52,769 --> 00:01:54,860
the person with the authority to commit.

28
00:02:00,650 --> 00:02:08,168
The approver sees the drafted rationale, their own approval limit, and the exact instruction, before anything leaves.

29
00:02:08,168 --> 00:02:11,060
Your systems stay authoritative for the work.

30
00:02:11,270 --> 00:02:14,645
One approval reference travels with every instruction.

31
00:02:14,645 --> 00:02:16,520
There is no auto-approve path.

32
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:25,545
Behind the screen, every stage of this asset's journey was run by Circularity's agents.

33
00:02:25,545 --> 00:02:32,730
Each line shows the agent, the tool it called, the system it reached, what it got, and the audit ID that proves it.

34
00:02:33,130 --> 00:02:34,333
Watch the counters:

35
00:02:34,333 --> 00:02:37,500
agents, tool calls, model calls and audit entries.

36
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,400
Every one of them is recorded.

37
00:02:43,270 --> 00:02:45,840
Where models come into play, it names them.

38
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:53,310
A vision model checks the inspection photos against the inspector's grade, and a survival model estimates the remaining life.

39
00:02:55,950 --> 00:03:02,447
The Opportunity Finder matches demand, prices every route with gradient-boosted models, and decides.

40
00:03:02,447 --> 00:03:06,930
Each model shows its measured error, so you know how far to trust it.

41
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:17,852
The Handoff Coordinator sends the approved plan into your order, maintenance and warehouse processes, and each one sends its own reference back.

42
00:03:17,852 --> 00:03:20,450
Then the actual result comes back on its own.

43
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:32,540
Finance confirms the outcome, and the Reconciler and the Analytics Explainer close the loop.

44
00:03:39,630 --> 00:03:47,190
Ninety-six hundred predicted, ninety-two thirty actual, explained line by line, and the model learns from the difference.

45
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:56,217
Circularity connects to what you already run:

46
00:03:56,217 --> 00:04:01,843
lease, ERP, asset management, repair, warehouse, service, quality and market data.

47
00:04:01,843 --> 00:04:04,930
Those systems keep owning their transactions.

48
00:04:08,760 --> 00:04:10,259
And it's open by design.

49
00:04:10,259 --> 00:04:16,129
Circularity uses your platforms' agent tools, and your own agents can call its governed tools.

50
00:04:16,129 --> 00:04:18,690
Every agent has a scope it cannot exceed.

51
00:04:22,850 --> 00:04:27,977
And you decide how far each agent may go, role by role and action by action:

52
00:04:27,977 --> 00:04:33,171
off, suggest, prepare, or act and notify, with a kill switch for every agent.

53
00:04:33,171 --> 00:04:35,600
Commitments always stop at a person.

54
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,397
Measured against current practice:

55
00:04:40,397 --> 00:04:48,340
thirty-seven percent more value recovered, one point seven million of spend avoided, and value realised twenty-two percent faster.

56
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:55,840
And because every decision is reconciled against its outcome, the forecasts get measurably better with every cycle.

57
00:04:57,510 --> 00:05:00,234
Start in shadow mode, beside your teams.

58
00:05:00,234 --> 00:05:04,524
Then one route, then the closed loop, then the whole portfolio.

59
00:05:04,524 --> 00:05:06,295
Your systems run the work.

60
00:05:06,295 --> 00:05:09,223
Circularity makes sure it's the right work.

61
00:05:09,223 --> 00:05:11,130
Agent-first, human-governed.
